---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const app = appBySlug('firepush')!;
const path = '/apps/firepush';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'apps/firepush');
const desc = description(site, 'apps/firepush');

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is Firepush a full Shopify email marketing platform?',
    answer: 'No. Firepush’s current vendor notice identifies it as a web-push app and says email and SMS campaigns are no longer offered. Evaluate required email journeys through a separate current sender.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does web push work for Shopify cart recovery?',
    answer: 'Evaluate cart recovery only with supported devices, valid push permission and reliable cart and purchase events. Choose a comparison that can estimate incremental margin. Browser mix and installation requirements affect eligible reach; there is no universal opt-in or recovery rate.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Firepush vs Omnisend push?',
    answer: 'Compare the exact events, channels, shared suppression behavior and all-in quotes for your intended setup. Test queue cancellation and purchase updates between tools. This page does not establish a current feature or price advantage for either vendor.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can Firepush replace Postscript?',
    answer: 'Not for SMS sending: Firepush no longer offers SMS campaigns. Web push is a separate channel with its own browser permission and reach. If replacing an SMS workflow, assess a current SMS sender rather than treating browser subscriptions as phone-marketing permission.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How coordinate Firepush with Klaviyo or Sequenzy?',
    answer: 'Assign one sender per purpose and verify purchase exits and current permission at dispatch. Tags can record state, but delayed writes or missing updates can leave stale jobs queued. Test failure alerts and cancellation before enabling both senders.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What causes push opt-in collapse?',
    answer: 'Frequent messages outside the purpose people requested can lead to revocations. Set purpose-specific frequency rules and monitor eligible reach, complaints and purchases. No board-game test or fixed percentage decline is established here.',
  },
  {
    question: 'When add Firepush to existing ESP?',
    answer: 'Consider an additional push layer when supported eligible reach and a controlled evaluation justify its maintenance and total cost. An email non-open or absent SMS opt-in is not push permission; verify the relevant permission and current purchase state independently.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Impression billing surprises?',
    answer: 'Confirm current billable units and included usage, then model overlapping restock and promotional sends. Calendar separation alone does not guarantee a lower bill; no doubled charge is established by the example.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Graduation signal?',
    answer: 'Reassess the stack when suppression reliability, required reporting or maintenance exceeds your available resources. Measure actual operating effort and validate alternatives before changing sender ownership; no fixed weekly-hours threshold applies.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/apps" class="text-sm font-bold text-[#9a5b16] hover:text-[#24170f]">← All tool reviews</a>
      <p class="catalog-kicker mt-6">Push + recovery</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{app.name} review for Shopify stores</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">
        Firepush’s current vendor notice identifies it as a web-push app and says email and SMS campaigns are no longer offered. Evaluate a short, purpose-specific browser alert alongside your existing email program. The useful buying question is whether supported, permissioned browser reach and incremental contribution justify another sender and queue; comparative entry costs are not established here.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#5d3a1d]">The examples below propose evaluations for a desktop-heavy board-game shop, a limited-pressing vinyl store and a mechanical keyboard startup. They are not observed tests: no recovery lift, opt-in change or order threshold is established. Compare added channel value with permission, maintenance and total cost requirements before adopting the layer.</p>
      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/apps/omnisend">Omnisend review</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/apps/recart">Recart review</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/use-cases/back-in-stock">Back-in-stock guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <p>Scope checked November 25, 2026: <a class="link" href="https://getfirepush.com/blog/targeted-email-marketing/">Firepush’s current notice</a> says the product is web push and no longer offers email or SMS campaigns. Its November 18 article update is not a documented channel-shutdown date. This current notice takes precedence over older listing descriptions; it is not a merchant performance test or a quote.</p>
    <TldrBox
      title="Verdict: Firepush for Shopify"
      picks={[
        { label: 'Channels', tool: 'Web push', reason: 'Current vendor notice: no email or SMS campaigns. Verify supported browsers and required events.' },
        { label: 'Pricing', tool: 'Current quote', reason: 'Confirm billable units, included usage and operating costs.' },
        { label: 'Strength', tool: 'Back-in-stock push', reason: 'A short alert for a requested limited-SKU restock — verify inventory before dispatch.' },
        { label: 'Tradeoff', tool: 'Segmentation', reason: 'Verify cross-sender purchase exits and queue cancellation in the intended setup.' },
        { label: 'Best for', tool: 'Additional alert layer', reason: 'Teams able to validate permission, queue ownership and added channel value.' },
      ]}
    />

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Web push as incremental recovery, not primary channel</h2>
      <p>A board-game shop could evaluate web push for eligible repeat visitors alongside email recovery. Choose timing from the purchase cycle, cancel reminders after purchase and compare against a suitable control. Platform-attributed carts alone do not prove incremental recovery or justify replacing an email platform.</p>
      <p>Assess actual browser, device and installation requirements before designing push enrollment. A vinyl restock alert could target people who requested that purpose, with stock rechecked before sending. Neither a universal Safari conversion ratio nor a sales result is established by this example.</p>
      <p>
        A proposed keyboard setup could schedule email before push. Use controlled records to purchase between touches, withdraw permission, delay the purchase event and fail the tag write. The later touch should cancel or enter a documented safe state; record the responsible system and repair steps.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Shopify integration depth and gaps</h2>
      <p>The current vendor notice establishes web push rather than email or SMS campaign sending. Confirm the exact recovery, browse, price-watch and restock events available in the intended installation before designing notification flows. An event checklist is a proposed test, not a guarantee that every trigger is included.</p>
      <p><strong>Evaluate:</strong> Cart recovery and limited-restock alerts where the required events and permissions are available. Obtain a current quote and validate setup effort rather than assuming low-volume billing or a sales-free installation.</p>
      <p><strong>Friction to test:</strong> Check suppression and purchase updates across Firepush and the external ESP, including queued messages. A historical purchase tag is not a current eligibility check. Confirm required segmentation and browser-notification controls; keep email and SMS jobs with their separately chosen current senders.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Pricing and impression spikes</h2>
      <p>Request the current plan terms, billable units and included channels. Model the same audience, send frequency and restock calendar across alternatives, including external ESP fees, SMS charges and operating time; historical entry prices are not a current quote.</p>
      <p><strong>Quiet month — board games:</strong> Model eligible audience, intended sends and matched all-in costs for an illustrative $89 cart. Include margin, discounts and returns; this example provides no measured incremental recovery or positive ROI.</p>
      <p><strong>Restock week — vinyl:</strong> Model restock and promotional sends to an illustrative 800-person eligible audience under the quoted billing rules. Overlapping campaigns may change usage, but neither a doubled bill nor savings from calendar separation is established.</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Coordination budget — keyboards:</strong> Record event mapping, monitoring, failed-write repair and weekly queue review effort. Compare a split stack with a consolidated candidate using matched channel coverage and a dated quote. Change architecture when required controls fail or maintenance exceeds the team’s budget.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Four workflow tests on Shopify</h2>
      <p><strong>1. Desktop cart push — board games.</strong> Test an illustrative $89 game cart using a supported browser and valid push permission. Set timing from the purchase cycle, recheck purchase state and compare incremental margin against a suitable control; no recovery percentage is established.</p>
      <p><strong>2. Back-in-stock — vinyl 500-copy restock.</strong> Evaluate alerts only for subscribers who requested that restock purpose. Verify stock before sending and distinguish attributed orders from additional orders caused by the alert; no sell-through result is established.</p>
      <p>
        <strong>3. Email coordination — keyboards.</strong> Propose email at hour two and push at hour six as test settings. Purchase between touches and confirm both current-state exclusion and cancellation of the queued push; the timing itself is not a suppression mechanism.</p>
      <p><strong>4. Push fatigue evaluation.</strong> Set purpose-specific frequency limits and monitor permission revocations, complaints and purchases. Compare a restrained recovery/restock schedule with any proposed promotional cadence; no opt-in loss or restoration rate is established.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Lifecycle, newsletters, and when to graduate</h2>
      <p>
        Keep welcome, replenishment and winback email requirements with a current email sender; Firepush no longer offers email campaigns. For drop announcements, define audience overlap and which channel owns the first alert. A six-hour gap does not prevent a duplicate offer or an ineligible send.</p>
      <p>Shipping updates and promotional recovery have different purposes. Assign an owner to each message and define cross-channel priority for delivery delays. A service update does not establish marketing permission; verify current channel eligibility and cancel conflicting queued promotions where the systems permit it.</p>
      <p>Evaluate alternatives when required channels, reporting or suppression cannot be maintained reliably within your staffing budget. Record actual coordination time and required fields; neither four weekly hours nor an order count establishes a universal migration threshold or compliance guarantee.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ledger-card mb-12">
      <p class="catalog-kicker">Frequency caps</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Firepush operating contract</h2>

      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Test prompt timing and placement within eligible supported traffic</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Set purpose-specific frequency limits and monitor revocations</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Back-in-stock push limited to waitlist segment with explicit opt-in</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Validate current purchase/suppression state and cancel stale queued messages</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Weekly review of opt-in rate trend — early warning before recovery collapses</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 mb-12">
      <div class="card">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Pros</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">
          {['Separate channel evaluation with documented owners', 'Preserve useful events and assets when changing senders'].map((s) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">+</span>{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Cons</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">
          {['Cross-tool dispatch controls require verification', 'Historical catalog labels do not establish current availability'].map((l) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">−</span>{l}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 mb-12">
      <div class="ledger-card">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Who should buy</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Desktop-heavy traffic with repeat visitors</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Limited-run restock urgency where push speed matters</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Budget covers a current matched quote and controlled channel evaluation</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Existing email setup leaves a distinct browser-alert requirement</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-card">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Who should skip</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Required browser or installation states do not support the planned reach</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Need one validated owner for the required lifecycle channels</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Need SMS sending, replies or escalation as a required channel</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Required suppression exceeds the validated integration or staffing capacity</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card mb-12">
      <p class="catalog-kicker">Compare alternatives</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Related Shopify email tools</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg font-bold">
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/omnisend">Omnisend review</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/recart">Recart review</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart guide</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-postscript">Omnisend vs Postscript</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- TARGETED_EXPANSION_v4 -->

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Push permission UX on Shopify themes</h2>
      <p>For a board-game shop, compare prompt placement and timing within eligible traffic using a predefined sample plan. A vinyl label could test a corner slide-in against a modal while recording acceptance, bounce and purchases. Measure theme performance before and after SDK changes; deferring a script does not itself prove that Core Web Vitals are preserved.</p>
      <p>For an illustrative 500-copy pressing, limit restock push to people who requested that message purpose. An imported email list is not push permission. Recheck stock and current suppression before sending; the scenario establishes no allocation sold or comparative opt-out rate.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- TARGETED_EXPANSION_v5 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="ledger-card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Safari limitations</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Mobile web push reality check</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">Validate current web-push requirements on the actual browsers, operating systems and installed-app states your audience uses. Measure eligible enrollment separately from total site traffic; this page provides no same-store Safari-to-Chrome ratio or observed opt-in result.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v6 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Firepush and Sequenzy email pairing</h2><p>For a proposed keyboard pairing, map customer identity across the email sender and push subscription. Record purchase events at the authoritative source, then test delayed tags, theme-script removal and replayed webhooks. Alert on missing updates and halt the affected journey until repaired. An order count does not predict reliability.</p><p>Use the current written billing terms to model subscriber counts, billable units and send frequency. Compare a restrained promotional calendar with the intended recovery schedule while measuring margin and revocations; this example establishes neither a 41% saving nor unchanged recovery.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v7 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Price drop</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Price drop push versus email</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">A board-game publisher could test a price-drop alert to people who requested price-watch messages. Compare eligible cohorts, timing and margin with a defined control. No push-versus-email conversion advantage is established, and price-watch permission should not be treated as general launch permission.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v8 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="ledger-card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Analytics</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Incremental push attribution</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">Predefine a suitable holdout and observation window for incremental recovery. Platform attribution may overlap email or include people who would purchase anyway. Estimate uncertainty and incremental margin after matched costs; no 3.1% or 4.2% result or finance approval is established.</p></div></section>

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">When web push belongs in a Shopify email stack</h2>
      <p>
        Use push for a concise requested alert when browser support and permission permit delivery. A board-game store can measure eligible research visitors separately from all traffic; a mobile-heavy camping store should inspect device and installation states before allocating budget. Compare incremental margin after operating costs rather than inferring a universal push-to-email opt-in ratio.</p>
      <p>Treat push, email and SMS as separate permission and queue domains. Define which system owns each purpose and validate current suppression and purchase state before sending. Non-opening is an unreliable signal for escalation; choose channel timing through an eligible test rather than assuming a two-hour delay or a universal sequence.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Three merchant scenarios: push done right and wrong</h2>
      <p><strong>Scenario A — Vinyl restock waitlist.</strong> For an illustrative 500-copy pressing, test a restock alert only with purpose-eligible push subscribers. Recheck inventory and compare incremental margin; this is a proposed workflow, not an observed thirty-minute sell-through result.</p>
      <p><strong>Scenario B — Mechanical keyboard GB close.</strong> Compare immediate and later-session enrollment prompts on supported devices. Track acceptance, bounce, product-page conversion and theme performance with a predefined sample plan. Neither doubled opt-in nor preserved Core Web Vitals is established here.</p>
      <p><strong>Scenario C — Pottery flash sale overload.</strong> Evaluate a restrained promotional cadence with separate recovery eligibility. Monitor revocations and purchases, then model billable usage from current terms. No opt-in collapse, recovery stability or cost saving is asserted for a real merchant.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Workflow tests before Firepush annual commit</h2>
      <p><strong>Test 1 — Opt-in UX variants.</strong> Compare a corner slide-in and center modal within eligible traffic using a predefined allocation and stopping plan. Record acceptance, bounce and purchase outcomes with uncertainty; no winning layout or 31% improvement is established.</p>
      <p><strong>Test 2 — Incremental holdout.</strong> Choose allocation and duration from eligible traffic, expected effect and purchase latency. Keep control exposure consistent across overlapping channels. Report incremental margin separately from platform-attributed recovery and include uncertainty and matched costs.</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Test 3 — Email collision.</strong> Create a controlled purchase while the second email is queued. Repeat with an expired push subscription and a failed purchase-state update. Record cancellation evidence, failure visibility and repair ownership; do not rely on a historical recovery tag alone.</p>
      <p><strong>Test 4 — Safari mobile reality.</strong> Validate enrollment and delivery on representative supported devices and installation states. Compare eligible opt-in and purchase outcomes within device cohorts before allocating budget; a universal three-to-one ratio is not established.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Buyer checklist and operating fit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Desktop or research-heavy traffic with session depth before purchase?</li>
        <li>Cart abandonment material enough to fund third channel after email and optional SMS?</li>
        <li>Team can maintain tag-based suppression with external ESP weekly?</li>
        <li>Permission prompt timing tested — not default first-second interrupt?</li>
        <li>Billing modeled from current written terms, planned cadence and eligible subscriber counts?</li>
        <li>Reassessment trigger based on measured maintenance, suppression reliability and available staffing?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Evaluate Firepush as an additional channel candidate against the required events, eligible reach, suppression reliability and total operating cost. Compare alternatives when coordination exceeds available staffing or required fields are unavailable. See <a class="link" href="/compare/firepush-vs-omnisend">Firepush vs Omnisend</a> for evaluation topics; no universal rank or order threshold establishes suitability.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="card">
      <p class="catalog-kicker">90-day proof plan</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Prove push increment before impression scale</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">Begin with permission UX and SDK performance checks on a staging theme. Validate cart-event identity, replay deduplication and queue cancellation with production sends disabled. Add a purpose-eligible restock or price-watch test only after those checks, then choose a holdout duration from traffic and purchase latency. Review incremental margin, current fees and maintenance time; the stages are an example, not a ninety-day promise.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-8">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-bold">
      <a class="link" href="/apps">All Shopify email tools →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparison hub →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/for/high-aov">High-AOV stores →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Firepush Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
